course: dictionary
lesson: 7553
title: Pregnant: a baby on the way, or a pause full of meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pregnant has two meanings. The first is about a woman or female animal with a baby growing inside her body before it is born. The second is about a silence. The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
explain: «Mum is pregnant, and the new baby is due in the spring.» The baby and the spring show that this is the first meaning. «The teacher asked a question, and there was a pregnant pause before anyone spoke.» The silence and the waiting show the second meaning: a quiet moment full of meaning, when everyone waits for what comes next.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. Does "a silence full of meaning" fit the pause? Yes. Does "a baby growing inside her body" fit Mum? Yes. The time a baby takes to grow is different for each animal, so read the sentence carefully.
fact: A woman or female animal is pregnant when a baby is growing inside her body before it is born.
fact: A pregnant pause is a silence full of meaning, when everyone waits for what comes next.
fact: «Pregnancy» is the noun: the time when a baby is growing inside its mother.
fact: A human pregnancy lasts about nine months, and a cat's lasts about two months.
fact: «An elephant mother is pregnant for about 22 months, the longest of any land animal.»
exercise: «An elephant mother is pregnant for about 22 months, the longest of any land animal.» Which land animal is pregnant the longest? | The dog | The cat | *The elephant | The human
exercise: «After the question, there was a pregnant pause.» What does pregnant mean here? | A loud noise | A baby growing inside someone | A long walk | *A silence full of meaning, as everyone waits
exercise: Chatty British slang: «Preggers» means which word? | Sleepy | *Pregnant | Hungry | Wet
test: «In the family way» is an old-fashioned way of saying what? | Lost | *Pregnant | Hungry | Married
test: Which word means the time a baby grows inside its mother? | Elephant | Pause | Pregnant | *Pregnancy
exam: «Trying for a baby» means attempting to get pregnant. Which word is closest in meaning to attempting? | Forgetting | Hiding | Sleeping | *Trying
